=============================================
 Inverse Complex Function Diagnostic
=============================================

Input z =  0.5 +  0.5i

--- C_ASIN ---
  sin(z)  =  0.5406126976 +  0.4573041201i
  asin(sin(z)) =  0.5 +  0.5i
  expected      = 0.5 + 0.5i

  asin(0.5+0i)  =  0.5235987902 +  0i
  expected       =  0.5235987756 + 0i

--- C_ACOS (control - should pass) ---
  cos(z)  =  0.9895848632 + -0.2498263866i
  acos(cos(z)) =  0.5000001192 +  0.4999999702i
  expected      = 0.5 + 0.5i

--- C_ATAN ---
  tan(z)  =  0.403896451 +  0.564083159i
  atan(tan(z)) =  0.4999999702 +  0.5i
  expected      = 0.5 + 0.5i

--- C_ASINH ---
  sinh(z) =  0.4573041201 +  0.5406126976i
  asinh(sinh(z)) =  0.5 +  0.5i
  expected        = 0.5 + 0.5i

  asinh(0+0i)  =  0 +  0i
  expected      = 0 + 0i

--- C_ACOSH ---
  cosh(z) =  0.9895848632 +  0.2498263866i
  acosh(cosh(z)) =  0.4999999702 +  0.5i
  expected        = 0.5 + 0.5i

  acosh(1+0i)  =  0 +  0i
  expected      = 0 + 0i

--- Direct inverse calls with computed inputs ---
  Computed sin(0.5+0.5i) =  1 +  0i
  asin(above) =  1.570796371 +  0i
  expected    = 0.5 + 0.5i

=============================================
 If values above show 0+0i instead of 0.5+0.5i,
 then the Pico SDK C library functions
 (casinf/catanf/casinhf/cacoshf) have bugs.
=============================================

